    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nExceptional Coastal Residence with 40.5 Acres in the Heart of North Mayo...\n\nSet on an elevated site overlooking the spectacular North Mayo coastline, this charming bungalow with extensive agricultural lands offers a rare opportunity to acquire a home in one of Ireland's most scenic locations. Situated at Killerduff, Ballycastle, Co. Mayo, just 1.2 km from Killerduff Pier along the renowned Wild Atlantic Way, the property enjoys breathtaking views across the countryside towards Downpatrick Head.\n\nBuilt in the late 1930s, the well-maintained bungalow extends to approximately 91.3 sq. m (983 sq. ft) and offers comfortable accommodation comprising an entrance porch with panoramic coastal views, a bright sitting room with solid-fuel fireplace and back boiler, dining room with open fireplace, kitchen with traditional solid-fuel range, family bathroom, and three generously sized bedrooms. The home benefits from oil-fired central heating, uPVC double-glazed windows, and an abundance of natural light throughout.\n\nOutside, the property is complemented by a spacious front garden, ample parking, and a range of useful agricultural sheds and outbuildings, making it ideal for farming, equestrian use, or those seeking a lifestyle property.\n\nThe lands extend to approximately 40.5 acres in total and are offered in the following lots:\n\n- Lot 1 (MY37935F): House on approximately 17.27 acres of mixed agricultural land with sheds and outbuildings.\n- Lot 2 (MY31590): Approximately 5.18 acres of agricultural land adjoining the house.\n- Lot 3 (MY20032): Approximately 7.85 acres of good-quality agricultural land.\n- Lot 4 (MY20032): Approximately 2.74 acres of good-quality agricultural land.\n- Lot 5 (MY20081): Approximately 7.46 acres of mixed agricultural land.\n\nAll lots are open to negotiation. The house can also be sold separately with 1 acre of land.\n\nLocated close to Ballycastle village, the property is within easy reach of some of Mayo's most celebrated attractions, including Downpatrick Head, the Céide Fields Visitor Centre, Ballinglen Museum of Art, and the stunning beaches and coastal walks that define this beautiful stretch of the Wild Atlantic Way.\n\nWhether you're seeking a family home, holiday retreat, working farm, or an investment in one of Ireland's most picturesque coastal regions, this exceptional property offers endless potential in an unrivalled setting.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the unique location, outstanding views, and exceptional opportunity on offer."
      },
